    "created_at": "2016-12-02T04:46:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-12-02T04:46:27Z",
    "body": "> The descriptors are always value descriptors with value: undefined, right?\r\n\r\nYes.\r\n\r\n@annevk, @domenic: @bholley and I can see no reason for the current setup other than it being an oversight; sane behavior would be to return these things from [[OwnPropertyKeys]].  So I'm going to implement accordingly in Gecko in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1321299 and write the web platform test accordingly too.  Please let me know ASAP if you can think of a reason I shouldn't do that.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
